ex_id": "pie-lex-dhegjhoxm", "role": "SUBJ"}, {"lex_id": "pie-lex-h1werHus", "role": "MOD", "head": 2}, {"lex_id": "pie-lex-sedos", "role": "PRED"}, {"lex_id": "pie-lex-deywos", "role": "IO", "num": "PL"}, {"lex_id": "pie-lex-h1esti", "role": "V", "verb": {"tense": "PRS", "mood": "IND", "voice": "ACT"}}]}]}, "cluster": "sky-father"}, "neologism": false, "secure_share": 0.6, "branches": 2, "notes": "Heaven and Earth are urvī́ sádmanī 'the two broad seats' (RV 1.185.6); Earth is ἕδος ἀσφαλές of the immortals (Hes. Th. 117f.) and εὐρυεδὴς χθών 'broad-seated earth' (Simonides); kṣā́m ... urvī́m = εὐρεῖα χθών. Ved. sádman- (*sed-mn̥) and Gk ἕδος (*sédos, = Ved. sádas-) are the same root. 'For the gods' is interpolated: Ved. devā́nām and Gk ἀθανάτων are different words."}
