}, "neologism": false, "secure_share": 0.5, "branches": 2, "notes": "εὐρεῖα χθών = Ved. kṣā́m ... urvī́m (West 2007 ch. 4, 'Attributes of Earth'); the Greek earth 'nourishes' (τρέφει, Il. 11.741). The verb and object come from the Gathic 'this earth that bears us' (Y. 38.1 imąm ... ząm ... yā nā̊ baraitī): bʰer- and nos are Indo-Iranian only, so interpolated."}
