"cluster": "sky-father"}, "neologism": false, "secure_share": 0.5, "branches": 2, "notes": "The heaven that Mazdā wears is stəhr-paēsah- 'star-ornamented' (Yt. 13.2–3; Av. paēsah- = *péyḱos exactly); Agni 'adorned the vault with stars' (RV 1.68.10, Ved. piś-); Euripides' ἀστέρων ποικίλματα (Hel. 1096, cited from West 2007 ch. 9) has the same root (cf. ποικίλον ἀστερόεντα, Il. 16.134, of a breastplate). 'Heaven' is h₂éḱmō (Av. asman- 'heaven', Ved. áśman- 'stone'): Iranian only, interpolated; copula interpolated."}
